#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:24
msgid "Match"
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:25
msgid "The published p= value matches the locally-stored public key. DKIM verification at receivers should succeed (assuming the message body is not modified in transit)."
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:29
msgid "Mismatch"
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:30
msgid "A DKIM record is published, but its p= value differs from the locally-stored public key. This typically means a key was regenerated locally without republishing the new DNS record, or the wrong record was published."
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:34
msgid "No record found"
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:35
msgid "DNS reports no TXT record at this name. Either the record has not been published yet, propagation has not completed, or the wrong name was used."
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:39
msgid "Record present but unparseable"
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:40
msgid "TXT records were returned at this name but none contained a valid v=DKIM1 / p= structure. Check the DNS provider for a malformed entry."
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:44
msgid "No local key"
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:45
msgid "There is no key stored locally to compare against. Generate a key pair first."
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:49
msgid "Misconfigured DNS — zone appended twice"
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:50
msgid "Your DNS provider has duplicated the zone in the record name. This usually happens when the full FQDN is pasted into the provider's \"Host\" or \"Name\" field, which then auto-appends the zone. Edit the Host field to omit the zone part — use just the \"Host name (recommended)\" value from the Setup tab."
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:54
msgid "Misconfigured DNS — missing _domainkey label"
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:55
msgid "A TXT record exists, but the \"_domainkey\" subdomain is missing from the name. The DKIM record name must include \"._domainkey.\" between the selector and the signing domain. Compare your DNS entry to the \"Host name (recommended)\" value on the Setup tab."
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:60
#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:71
msgid "Check DNS record"
msgstr ""

#: admin-templates/partials/verify-dns-check.php:63
msgid "Performs a fresh DNS lookup of <selector>._domainkey.<signing-domain> and compares the published p= value to the locally-stored public key. The result is not cached — propagation issues are the most common DNS gotcha and a fresh lookup is cheap."
msgstr ""

